      "assessment": "# Audit Notes \u2014 ShanhaiBeasts (BSC, `0xFF47\u2026ee15`)\n\n**Status: preliminary, source-excerpt only.** The excerpt is truncated mid-`_head`, so several functions (`_b64`, `_dec`, full `tokenURI`) are not visible. Findings below are split into *validated from the shown code* vs *scanner noise* vs *needs full source*.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Scanner findings \u2014 triage\n\n### `weak-prng` (High/Medium) \u2014 **partially valid, low financial impact**\n`_mintOne` derives species from `keccak256(abi.encode(seed, id)) % 10`, where `seed` is built from `block.prevrandao`, `blockhash(block.number-1)`, `msg.sender`, and `id`.\n\n- **Real weakness:** `prevrandao` on BSC is validator-influenced and `blockhash` is public; a miner/validator or a bundler can bias or predict species. Species is cosmetic (art only) \u2014 no on-chain gameplay, no rarity-linked payout in the shown code \u2014 so **financial impact is limited to secondary-market rarity sniping**, not fund loss.\n- **Mitigating:** `id` increments per token, so a single tx produces a deterministic sequence; a minter cannot freely re-roll within one tx without paying for more slots.\n- **Not a fund-drain vector.** Treat as a fairness/rarity-integrity issue, not a critical.\n\n### `incorrect-equality` \u00d710 \u2014 **false positives**\nAll flagged `==` comparisons are on `uint256` tier/species selectors in pure view/art functions (`_beast`, `_tierName`, `_frame`, `_stars`, `_bg`, `_svg`). These are intentional dispatch on small enums, not balance checks. **No action.**\n\n### `low-level-call` (ShanhaiBeasts.sol:137) \u2014 **validated, low risk**\n```solidity\n(bool ok, ) = payable(creator).call{value: msg.value}(\"\");\nif (!ok) revert TransferFailed();\n```\n- Return value **is** checked; failure reverts the whole mint. \n- **Reentrancy:** state (`slotsMinted`, `_balances`, `totalSupply`, `_tok`) is fully updated **before** the call, and the call is the last action. A malicious `creator` could reenter `mint`, but `creator` is immutable and set at deploy \u2014 only a risk if the deployer is adversarial toward themselves. **No exploitable reentrancy for third parties.**\n- **Griefing:** if `creator` is a contract that rejects BNB, all paid mints revert. Free mint (`msg.value == 0`) skips the call, so it still works. This is a **liveness risk for paid mints**, not theft.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Issues found in the shown source (not flagged by scanner)\n\n### A. `tokensOfOwner` is O(totalSupply) and can exceed block gas limit \u2014 **Medium (DoS on view)**\n```solidity\nfor (uint256 i = 1; i <= ts && j < n; ++i) { ... }\n```\nAt 5,000 supply this is ~5,000 SLOADs per call. Off-chain callers (marketplaces, wallets) may hit RPC gas caps. **View-only; no on-chain funds at risk.** Recommend documenting or paginating.\n\n### B. `_svg` fixed 32,000-byte buffer \u2014 **Medium (metadata DoS)**\n`b = new bytes(32000)` with manual `mstore(b, p)` length rewrite. If any tier/species combination writes past 32,000 bytes, the `mstore` corrupts adjacent memory or the returned length is wrong, producing malformed `tokenURI`. The `_w` helper copies 32-byte words with slack, so **overflow is plausible for Legendary (tier 3) with dense sprites + stars + aura paths**. This is a **metadata/art integrity bug**, not a fund bug, but it can brick `tokenURI` for specific tokens. **Needs full-source + fuzz validation** (see \u00a74).\n\n### C. `_stars` reads `g[y*32 + x \u00b1 1/32]` without bounds guard \u2014 **Low/Medium**\n```solidity\nbool big = ... && g[y * 32 + x - 1] == 0 && g[y * 32 + x + 1] == 0 && g[y * 32 + x - 32] == 0 && g[y * 32 + x + 32] == 0;\n```\n`x \u2208 [4,27]`, `y \u2208 [4,27]`, so indices stay in `[0,1023]` **given the current constants**. Safe today, but fragile if constants change. Note `x-1`/`x+1` are fine; the `-32`/`+32` are fine at these bounds. **Informational.**\n\n### D. `_grid` ring pass reads `g[c-1]`, `g[c+1]`, `g[c-32]`, `g[c+32]` for `x,y \u2208 [1,30]` \u2014 **safe**, but same fragility note.\n\n### E. `quote` / `mint` slot accounting \u2014 **validated correct**\n`getsFree = s == 0`; `z = s + (getsFree?1:0) + paid`; bonuses added when crossing `RARE_AT`/`LEGENDARY_AT`. `tokens` in `quote` matches the number of `_mintOne` calls in `mint` (free + paid + up to 2 bonuses). `totalSupply + tokens > MAX_SUPPLY` check uses the same `tokens`. **Consistent.** One subtlety: `quote` reverts `WalletLimit` if `paid > 30` even when `s > 0`; that's a UX quirk, not a bug.\n\n### F. `mint` bonus double-count edge \u2014 **validated safe**\nIf `s < 10` and `z \u2265 10`, one Rare added; if `s < 30` and `z \u2265 30`, one Legendary added. A single call crossing both thresholds (e.g., `s=9, paid=21 \u2192 z=30`) adds **both** bonuses, and `quote` also adds both. Consistent. `slotsMinted` caps at 30, so bonuses can't be re-triggered.\n\n### G. ERC-721 conformance gaps \u2014 **Low**\n- `supportsInterface` is `pure` and hardcodes `0x01ffc9a7, 0x80ac58cd, 0x5b5e139f, 0x2a55205a`. It does **not** return true for `0xffffffff` (ERC-165 requires `supportsInterface(0xffffffff) == false`, which is satisfied) \u2014 OK.\n- `transferFrom` does not check `to != address(0)` before `_balances[to] += 1`? It **does** (`if (to == address(0)) revert ZeroAddress();`). OK.\n- `approve` allows approving `address(0)` (clears) \u2014 standard.\n- No `_exists`/`tokenURI` revert for burned tokens \u2014 there is no burn. OK.\n- `safeTransferFrom` reentrancy: `transferFrom` completes state changes before the receiver callback; standard and safe.\n\n### H. `royaltyInfo` ignores `tokenId` and `salePrice == 0` \u2014 **Informational**\nReturns `(creator, salePrice*100/10000)`. Fine for EIP-2981.\n\n### I. Mint window / supply \u2014 **validated**\n`mintEnd = mintStart + 5 days`; `mint` checks `block.timestamp < mintEnd`. `remaining()` and `mintOpen()` consistent. No admin, no pause, no withdraw \u2014 matches the doc comment. **No privileged rug vector in shown code.**\n\n---\n\n## 3. Assumptions to verify against full source / on-chain\n\n1. `AGENT_ID` at `0",
